{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3182","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3182","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3182\",\"parent_revision\":\"8a07536782cb4676f5afd1f8496316bc11b661ee\",\"root_revision\":\"8d6d511f9b31c922774f61a3c27842d4c91609ad668155452ee6bb985b79edc9\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-23\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`backlog_add` can complete with `item_ref: \\\"\\\"` \u2014 no GitHub issue created \u2014 while returning a success-shaped result. The caller receives a populated dict and no error.\\n\\nObserved in CI on `main`, run 32624257966, job \\\"Python / E2E live tests\\\":\\n\\n```\\nplugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py:196: in test_l1_add_with_real_issue\\n    assert item_ref.startswith(\\\"#\\\"), f\\\"Expected item_ref like '#N', got: {item_ref!r}\\\"\\nE   AssertionError: Expected item_ref like '#N', got: ''\\n\\nplugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py:318: in test_l11_resolve_alternative_end\\n    l11_issue_num = int(create_result[\\\"item_ref\\\"].lstrip(\\\"#\\\"))\\nE   ValueError: invalid literal for int() with base 10: ''\\n```\\n\\nTwo symptoms, one defect. The remaining lifecycle tests then skip on the `l1_ok` sentinel, and two more pass only because they assert types rather than values.\\n\\nWhy the cause is still unknown, which is the substance of this item: `operations._try_create_github_issue` (around line 1377) returns `None` on either `try_get_github(...) is None` (\\\"GitHub unavailable\\\") or a caught `GithubException`/`BacklogError` (\\\"Issue creation failed: {e}\\\"). Both are recorded only via `out.warn(...)`. The reason therefore lives in `result[\\\"warnings\\\"]`, and neither test assertion includes it, so roughly four weeks of CI logs contain no information about why creation failed.\\n\\nThis is the failure shape `.claude/rules/silent-failure-prevention.md` prohibits directly: a write operation that does not report what changed, and a branch on an input condition whose fallback neither acts nor errors. An agent calling `backlog_add` cannot distinguish \\\"issue created\\\" from \\\"issue not created, item exists locally only\\\".\\n\\nNot caused by any recent change. Verified independently: every Code Quality run on `main` back through 2026-08-20 failed, including commits well before the recent backlog_core work (58df37b85, 79962289b, d22c524e6, 0a2ca9177). A subagent sampled e2e job conclusions on `main` on 2026-07-28, 08-06, 08-10 through 08-13, and every run from 08-14 to 08-23 \u2014 all failure, zero successes, so at least four weeks.\\n\\nThe symptom text changed once without the defect changing. Before 2026-08-18 it read `Expected item_ref in result, got: [...]` with `'reference': 'p1-mcp-test-<uuid>-live-test-item'` \u2014 the local-only fallback. PR #3160 made `item_ref` always present, so it became `got: ''`. Same bug throughout.\\n\\nRuled out as causes, with evidence: not a flake (20+ consecutive identical failures; the fixture uses a fresh tmp dir, a per-run UUID prefix and `force=True`); not rate limiting or auth rejection (step completes in 12.4s, no 403 or 429); not leftover state; not run contention. The job's token carries `Issues: write`.\\n\\nUser-provided context: a subagent's suggested cheapest first move is to include `result[\\\"warnings\\\"]` and `result[\\\"errors\\\"]` in the test assertion message, so the next CI run reports the actual cause \u2014 but that is a diagnostic aid, and the defect to fix is that a failed create is not surfaced to the caller at all. Whether the right contract is raising, an explicit status field, or something else is design work for grooming.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T00:49:34.188985Z</sub>\\n\\n**verdict:** VERIFIED\\n\\n**Claim 1: `_try_create_github_issue` returns `None` on `try_get_github(...) is None` or caught exception, recorded only via `out.warn(...)`**\\n- **evidence:** operations.py lines 1444\u20131463 show `_try_create_github_issue` returns `None` on line 1458 (`try_get_github` returning `None`) and line 1463 (caught `GithubException`/`BacklogError`). Both failures record the reason to `out.warn()` only (lines 1457, 1462).\\n- **source:** `/Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py:1444\u20131463`\\n\\n**Claim 2: `_try_create_backend_issue_ref` converts that `None` into empty string `\\\"\\\"` with no separate error signal**\\n- **evidence:** operations.py line 1499 returns `f\\\"#{issue_num}\\\" if issue_num else \\\"\\\"`. When `_try_create_github_issue` returns `None` (line 1498), the expression evaluates to empty string. No error field or separate signal is populated in the return value.\\n- **source:** `/Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py:1498\u20131499`\\n\\n**Claim 3: `BacklogAddResponse` has unused `error: str | None` field designed for exactly this signal, left `None` on this failure path**\\n- **evidence:** tool_responses.py line 116 shows `FallibleToolResponse` base class declares `error: str | None = None`. BacklogAddResponse (line 212) inherits from FallibleToolResponse. Tracing the code path: `backlog_add` (server.py) calls `operations.add_item()`, which calls `_try_create_backend_issue_ref()` at line ~1390. The response is never populated with the error; failure only records warnings in `out` dict.\\n- **source:** `/Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tool_responses.py:116,212` and `/Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` (pre-PR #3160 pattern where `backlog_add` returned `{\\\"error\\\": str(e)}` on BacklogError)\\n\\n**Claim 4: PR #3160 changed symptom text without changing defect; defect predates 2026-08-14 CI failures**\\n- **evidence:** PR #3160 (commit d837e171e, merged 2026-08-23) changed test assertions in test_live_validation.py: before the change, the test checked for `issue_num` field; after, it checks `item_ref.startswith(\\\"#\\\")`. The change only modified how the test reads the response, not the underlying `_try_create_github_issue`/`_try_create_backend_issue_ref` functions\u2014both are identical before and after PR #3160. Commit 765262e89 (Aug 12, 2026) introduced the `item_ref` field and changed response shape, predating PR #3160 and the reported CI failures (~Aug 14 onward). The defect (_try_create_backend_issue_ref returning empty string on failure without populating error) existed at or before commit 765262e89.\\n- **source:** `git log --oneline | grep \\\"3160\\\\|765262e89\\\"` and `git show d837e171e^:operations.py` vs. `git show d837e171e:operations.py` (functions identical)\\n\\n**Claim 5: Failure violates `rules/silent-failure-prevention.md` rule**\\n- **evidence:** rules/silent-failure-prevention.md section \\\"Branching on Input Values Requires an Explicit Fallback\\\" (lines 40\u201367) states: \\\"Every `if`/`elif` chain or match on an input value must have a final branch that either acts or errors. Falling through to `return unchanged` without logging is a silent data loss bug. If no fallback action is possible, raise or warn.\\\" The path `_try_create_backend_issue_ref` \u2192 `_try_create_github_issue` returns `None` on failure with only `out.warn()` (which the caller can ignore), then converts to empty string `\\\"\\\"` with no error signal to the MCP caller. The caller (test, agent, CLI) receives a success-shaped response with `item_ref: \\\"\\\"` and cannot distinguish \\\"issue created\\\" from \\\"issue not created.\\\" This violates the rule's requirement for an explicit fallback that \\\"either acts or errors.\\\"\\n- **source:** `/Users/jamienelson/repos/claude_skills/rules/silent-failure-prevention.md:40\u201367`\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T00:44:22.114047Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: fix: backlog_add returns an empty item_ref when issue creation fails, and the reason reaches no caller\\nDate: 2026-09-04\\nGoal: Make backlog_add surface why issue creation failed instead of returning a success-shaped empty item_ref.\\nConditions:\\n1. Defect is still present in current code \u2014 `_try_create_github_issue`/`_try_create_backend_issue_ref` (operations.py:1444-1499) record failure only via `out.warn()` | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. `BacklogAddResponse` already has an unused `error: str | None` field (tool_responses.py:216) designed for exactly this signal, left `None` on this path | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. Repo convention for this exact shape is documented in rules/silent-failure-prevention.md: \\\"if no fallback action is possible, raise or warn\\\" | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. Blast radius of populating `error`/changing the empty-string contract \u2014 which CLI, MCP, and test callers key off `item_ref == \\\"\\\"` today | Status: DERIVABLE\\n5. Whether the beads-backend sibling path (string-ID branch of `_try_create_backend_issue_ref`) shares the identical silent-failure shape | Status: DERIVABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 3\\nDERIVABLE count: 2\\nMISSING count: 0\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T00:58:59.032244Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: fix: backlog_add returns an empty item_ref when issue creation fails, and the reason reaches no caller\\nDate: 2026-09-04\\nGoal: Make backlog_add surface why issue creation failed instead of returning a success-shaped empty item_ref.\\nConditions:\\n1. Defect is still present in current code \u2014 `_try_create_github_issue`/`_try_create_backend_issue_ref` (operations.py:1444-1499) record failure only via `out.warn()` | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-Check claim 1/2 (operations.py:1444-1463, 1498-1499)\\n2. `BacklogAddResponse` already has an unused `error: str | None` field (tool_responses.py:216) designed for exactly this signal, left `None` on this path | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-Check claim 3 (tool_responses.py:116,212)\\n3. Repo convention for this exact shape is documented in rules/silent-failure-prevention.md: \\\"if no fallback action is possible, raise or warn\\\" | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Fact-Check claim 5 (rules/silent-failure-prevention.md:40-67)\\n4. Blast radius of populating `error`/changing the empty-string contract \u2014 which CLI, MCP, and test callers key off `item_ref == \\\"\\\"` today | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Impact Radius \u2014 MCP tool `backlog_add` (server.py:1377-1405), CLI `backlog add` (sam_schema/backlog.py:38-73), doc consumer create/start.md:156-192, and test_backlog_core_operations.py:419-431 which codifies today's broken contract and will need to change\\n5. Whether the beads-backend sibling path (string-ID branch of `_try_create_backend_issue_ref`) shares the identical silent-failure shape | Snapshot: DERIVABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Impact Radius \u2014 `TestAddItemBeadsBackend` (test_backlog_core_operations.py:565-650) proves beads already raises `ContentUnavailableError` on creation failure; only the GitHub/sqlite/memory integer-ID path is broken\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 4: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by impact-analyst \u2014 cite: server.py:1377-1405, sam_schema/backlog.py:38-73, create/start.md:156-192, test_backlog_core_operations.py:419-431)\\n- Condition 5: DERIVABLE \u2192 AVAILABLE (resolved by impact-analyst \u2014 cite: test_backlog_core_operations.py:565-650, beads backend already raises correctly)\\n- No REFUTED claims in Fact-Check (all 5 claims VERIFIED); no SCOPE_EXPANSION in Impact Radius; Design Intent Alignment verdict NOT_APPLICABLE (straightforward defect fix, no mission-alignment question)\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Issue Classification\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T00:56:25.635014Z</sub>\\n\\n**Type:** defect\\n\\n**Rationale:** The item describes a traceable, reproducible failure with a clear cause chain:\\n- Symptom: `backlog_add` returns `item_ref: \\\"\\\"` instead of a GitHub issue number, and the caller cannot distinguish success from failure.\\n- Root cause: `_try_create_backend_issue_ref()` (operations.py:1499) silently converts `None` from `_try_create_github_issue()` into an empty string without populating the `error` field or raising.\\n- Evidence: Fact-Check section independently verified five claims with file paths and line numbers; Impact Radius maps all code producers, consumers, and tests.\\n- Precedent: The beads backend path (already raises `ContentUnavailableError` on this failure) provides the target contract shape.\\n- Standards violation: The defect violates `rules/silent-failure-prevention.md` (\\\"Branching on Input Values Requires an Explicit Fallback\\\"); the failure path returns a success-shaped response with no error signal.\\n\\n**Analysis Method:** The existing evidence chain in the Description is unusually thorough and independently verified by the Fact-Check section (CI run IDs, ruled-out causes, function/line citations, confirmation of defect predating PR #3160). Root-cause analysis builds directly from this existing chain rather than re-running find-cause, since all key citations in the description have been re-verified against current source code.\\n\\n**Scenario Target:** Any agent or CLI command calling `backlog_add` (or the underlying `operations.add_item()`) will fail silently when GitHub issue creation is unavailable or fails. The caller receives a populated dict with no error signal and cannot proceed correctly with the next step in the backlog workflow. CI tests fail with opaque assertion errors, providing no diagnostic information about why creation failed.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T01:02:59.595380Z</sub>\\n\\n<details><summary>struck: 2026-09-04T01:56:26.031833Z \u2014 Architecture and task-decomposition phases found this section listed a file that needs no change (tool_responses.py \u2014 the error field already exists) and understated what test_live_validation.py:318 actually needs.</summary>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 `_try_create_github_issue()` (~1444-1463), `_try_create_backend_issue_ref()` (~1466-1499), `add_item()` (~1528-1636)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tool_responses.py` \u2014 `FallibleToolResponse` (~113-117), `BacklogAddResponse` (~212)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 MCP tool `backlog_add` (~1377-1405)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/backlog.py` \u2014 CLI `backlog add` (~38-73)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` \u2014 `test_add_item_item_ref_empty_when_no_github_issue` (~419-431), `TestAddItemBeadsBackend` (~565-650)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py` \u2014 `test_l1_add_with_real_issue` (~196), `test_l11_resolve_alternative_end` (~318)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md` (~156-192) \u2014 only needs a change if the caller-facing contract shape adds a branch the doc must describe\\n</details>\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T01:56:26.031866Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 `_try_create_github_issue()` (~1444-1463), `_try_create_backend_issue_ref()` (~1466-1499), `add_item()` (~1528-1636)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 MCP tool `backlog_add` (~1377-1405) \u2014 docstring-only update; no code change (`_respond` already forwards an `error` key from the result dict onto `BacklogAddResponse.error`)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/backlog.py` \u2014 CLI `backlog add` (~38-76) \u2014 one added exit-code check\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` \u2014 modify `test_add_item_item_ref_empty_when_no_github_issue` (~419-431), add `test_add_item_error_set_when_issue_creation_raises`, verify unchanged: `test_add_item_local_only_pending_state_visible_via_list_and_view` (~435-459), `TestAddItemBeadsBackend` (~565-650)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py` \u2014 `test_l1_add_with_real_issue` (~196): amend the existing assertion message to include `result.get(\\\"error\\\")`. `test_l11_resolve_alternative_end` (~318-320): this line has no assertion today (`l11_issue_num = int(create_result[\\\"item_ref\\\"].lstrip(\\\"#\\\"))`, the bare `ValueError` in this item's Description) \u2014 needs a new guard assertion added before the `int()` call, not a message edit.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md` \u2014 Step 5 (~155-158) gains a failure branch, Completion criteria (~189-193) gains a qualifying parenthetical; exact replacement text is in `plan/architect-backlog-add-silent-failure.md`'s Documentation contract section. This file DOES need a change \u2014 earlier wording (\\\"only needs a change if...\\\") was superseded once the architecture phase confirmed the contract does add exactly this branch.\\n\\nCorrection (2026-09-04, post-task-decomposition): removed `tool_responses.py` (`FallibleToolResponse`/`BacklogAddResponse`) \u2014 the architecture phase confirmed `error: str | None = None` already exists there and needs no change. See `plan/architect-backlog-add-silent-failure.md`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Resources\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T01:02:59.595397Z</sub>\\n\\n- `rules/silent-failure-prevention.md` (~40-67) \u2014 the standing convention this defect violates (\\\"every branch must either act or error\\\"); the authority planning should consult when choosing the fix's contract shape.\\n- The beads (string-ID) backend path in `operations.py` (~1486-1497), which already raises `ContentUnavailableError` on equivalent failure \u2014 an existing in-repo precedent for what \\\"surfaced correctly\\\" looks like on the sibling code path.\\n- PR #3160 (commit d837e171e) and commit 765262e89 \u2014 history showing the defect predates both and that only test-assertion text changed, useful context if planning needs to confirm nothing about the underlying functions shifted.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T01:02:59.595300Z</sub>\\n\\n- CI signal integrity: every \\\"Python / E2E live tests\\\" and \\\"Code Quality\\\" run on `main` has been affected for 4+ weeks; failures give no information about root cause, and passing lifecycle tests downstream of the broken assertion are only passing because they check types rather than values (weakened confidence in the whole suite's signal).\\n- Callers of `backlog_add` / `operations.add_item()` on the GitHub, sqlite, and memory backends (both the MCP tool at server.py and the CLI command at sam_schema/backlog.py) cannot distinguish \\\"issue created\\\" from \\\"issue not created, item exists locally only\\\" \u2014 any agent or script driving these interfaces can silently proceed as if an issue exists when it does not.\\n- One documented consumer workflow (`skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md`, \\\"Step 5: Use `item_ref` from the response\\\") has no branch for this failure case today.\\n- Not affected: the beads (string-ID) backend path, which already raises `ContentUnavailableError` on equivalent failure \u2014 confirmed by `TestAddItemBeadsBackend`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T00:50:39.192670Z</sub>\\n\\n**Code \u2014 Producers**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py:1444` `_try_create_github_issue()` \u2014 returns `None` on either `try_get_github()` returning `None` (\\\"GitHub unavailable\\\") or a caught `GithubException`/`BacklogError`, recording the reason only via `out.warn()`. This is the source of the lost reason string.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py:1466` `_try_create_backend_issue_ref()` \u2014 dispatches beads vs. integer-ID backends; on the integer-ID path it collapses `_try_create_github_issue`'s `None` to `\\\"\\\"`, discarding the reason a second time. Docstring at 1476-1485 already documents the empty-string contract in detail.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py:1528` `add_item()` \u2014 builds the result dict (`title`, `priority`, `reference`, `file_path`, `item_ref`) at lines 1626-1636; there is no `error` key on this success-shaped return, only `out.to_dict()`'s `messages`/`warnings`/`errors`, which the MCP layer keeps separate from the typed `error` field (see server.py below). Any fix touches this dict-construction site.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tool_responses.py:212` `BacklogAddResponse` \u2014 inherits `error: str | None` from `FallibleToolResponse` (tool_responses.py:113-117). This field is the \\\"already AVAILABLE\\\" fix surface named in RT-ICA condition 2: it is populated only in server.py's `except BacklogError` arm, never on the not-raised, empty-`item_ref` path.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py:1377-1405` MCP tool `backlog_add` \u2014 calls `operations.add_item` then `_respond(BacklogAddResponse, {**result, **out.to_dict()})`; `error` is left unset here because no exception is raised for this failure mode, so the typed response's own error channel goes unused exactly on the path that needs it.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/backlog.py:38-73` CLI `backlog add` (Typer) \u2014 calls `operations.add_item` directly and re-emits via `_emit()`, which prints `output.warnings` to stderr but still exits 0 with `item_ref: \\\"\\\"` in the JSON payload. Same blind spot, second call site \u2014 a fix in `add_item`/`_try_create_backend_issue_ref` alone covers both the MCP tool and this CLI command since they share the one function.\\n\\n**Code \u2014 Consumers**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md:156-192` \\\"Step 5: Use `item_ref` from the response\\\" \u2014 the one workflow doc that programmatically consumes `backlog_add`'s return contract (\\\"The `backlog_add` response contains `item_ref` \u2014 use that value directly for all downstream workflows\\\"). It has no branch for the empty-`item_ref`/failure case today; whatever contract shape grooming picks (raise, explicit status, populate `error`), this step needs a corresponding \\\"if creation failed\\\" branch.\\n- No other skill, agent, or hook reads `result[\\\"item_ref\\\"]` or `BacklogAddResponse.error` from `backlog_add`/`add_item` \u2014 confirmed by tracing every non-test call site of `add_item` (CLI and MCP tool above are the only two production callers).\\n\\n**Code \u2014 Other References (naming collision, not in scope)**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py:573` \u2014 `ContentDuplicateMatch.item_ref`, used in duplicate-detection error messages (`_check_for_duplicates`). Same field name, unrelated concern (an existing item's reference shown in a \\\"possible duplicate\\\" message, not `add_item`'s return value). Several agent/skill docs (e.g. `agents/backlog-item-groomer.md`) also use `item_ref` purely as a generic \\\"selector\\\" parameter name in their own prompts \u2014 unrelated to this contract. Flagging so grooming/planning doesn't chase these as callers.\\n\\n**Documentation**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/create/start.md` \u2014 see Consumers above; the only doc that specifies the response contract's consumption pattern. Needs a matching update if the contract shape changes.\\n- No other file under `plugins/development-harness/docs/` or `backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` documents the `add_item`/`backlog_add` return contract itself (ARCHITECTURE.md:404 only documents the unrelated `ContentDuplicateMatch.item_ref`).\\n\\n**Configuration/CI**\\n- No CI workflow YAML, label config, or milestone config references this contract directly. The relevant CI surface is behavioral, not configuration: the \\\"Python / E2E live tests\\\" job (GitHub Actions) runs `test_live_validation.py`, whose `test_l1_add_with_real_issue` (line 196) and `test_l11_resolve_alternative_end` (line 318) are the two failing assertions named in the item description, plus downstream lifecycle tests that skip on the `l1_ok` sentinel. Fixing the contract should make these tests either pass or fail with an informative reason \u2014 no CI file edits are needed for the fix itself, only for the test assertions in `test_live_validation.py`.\\n\\n**Agent Instructions**\\n- No agent instruction file (`plugins/development-harness/agents/*.md`) branches on `backlog_add`'s `item_ref` or `error` fields. The apparent hits for `item_ref` in `agents/backlog-item-groomer.md`, `agents/classifier.md`, `agents/fact-checker.md`, `agents/rtica-assessor.md`, `agents/technical-researcher.md` are all the unrelated generic-selector usage described above (confirmed by reading each hit in context) \u2014 none of them consume the `add_item`/`backlog_add` return value.\\n- `rules/silent-failure-prevention.md` \u2014 not agent instructions to change, but the standing convention this defect violates (\\\"if no fallback action is possible, raise or warn\\\"); grooming/planning should re-read it when choosing the fix's exact contract shape (raise vs. explicit `error` field vs. something else), since the item explicitly leaves that design decision open.\\n\\n**Systems Inventory**\\n- Backend abstraction: only the integer-ID path (`_try_create_github_issue` \u2192 GitHub, and by extension sqlite/memory backends that share `_try_create_backend_issue_ref`'s integer-ID branch) exhibits the silent-failure shape. The beads (string-ID) sibling path already raises `ContentUnavailableError` from `BeadsBackend.put_work_item` when `create_beads_issue_for_item` fails \u2014 see Tests below. This resolves RT-ICA condition 5: the shape is **not** shared across backends; only the GitHub/sqlite/memory branch needs fixing.\\n- Two production call sites of `add_item`: the MCP tool `backlog_add` (server.py) and the CLI command `backlog add` (sam_schema/backlog.py). Both inherit whatever fix lands in `operations.add_item`/`_try_create_backend_issue_ref` \u2014 no separate fix needed per call site.\\n- Test suites touching this contract: `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_operations.py` (mocked unit tests, see below) and `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_live_validation.py` (the live E2E suite failing in CI).\\n\\n**Ecosystem Completeness Checklist**\\n- Producers: \u2705 found and enumerated (2 operations.py functions, 1 response model, 2 call sites).\\n- Consumers: \u2705 found (1 workflow doc); confirmed no other skill/agent/hook consumes the field.\\n- Tests: \u2705 found and consequential, not just discoverable \u2014\\n  - `test_backlog_core_operations.py:419-431` `test_add_item_item_ref_empty_when_no_github_issue` explicitly asserts `result[\\\"item_ref\\\"] == \\\"\\\"` as the *entire* signal on failure. This test codifies today's contract and **must be updated, not just supplemented**, by whatever fix grooming selects \u2014 it will start failing (or need reinterpretation) the moment `add_item` starts also raising/erroring on this path.\\n  - `test_backlog_core_operations.py:565-650` class `TestAddItemBeadsBackend` (3 tests) \u2014 proves the beads path already raises `ContentUnavailableError` rather than silently returning `\\\"\\\"`; use this as the target shape/precedent when the integer-ID path is fixed, and as evidence for RT-ICA condition 5 above.\\n  - `test_live_validation.py:196,318` \u2014 the originally failing CI assertions; the fix's acceptance criteria should include these going from opaque failure to either passing or raising/reporting the real reason.\\n- Documentation: \u2705 found (1 file); confirmed no broader doc surface.\\n- Configuration/CI: \u2705 checked; no config changes in radius, one named CI job is the observable surface.\\n- Agent instructions: \u2705 checked; none apply \u2014 naming collisions ruled out by reading each hit.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Dependencies\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T01:02:59.595415Z</sub>\\n\\nNone identified. Impact Radius found no CI configuration, agent instruction file, or other in-flight work that depends on or conflicts with this fix; the two production call sites (MCP tool and CLI) both route through the same underlying function, so no separate coordination is needed between them.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Priority\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T01:02:59.595276Z</sub>\\n\\nP1 (already set, confirmed appropriate). This is a live, currently-active defect, not a hypothetical: every relevant CI job on `main` has been failing for at least four weeks because of it, and each failure carries zero diagnostic information about the real cause. It also violates a standing repository convention (`rules/silent-failure-prevention.md`) rather than being a new gap \u2014 the fallback-must-act-or-error rule is being broken today, in production code paths (MCP tool and CLI), not just in tests.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Benefits\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T01:02:59.595320Z</sub>\\n\\n- Restores an actual pass/fail signal to the \\\"Python / E2E live tests\\\" and \\\"Code Quality\\\" CI jobs, ending 4+ weeks of opaque, uninformative failures.\\n- Lets any caller (agent, CLI user, workflow) of `backlog_add`/`add_item` distinguish a created issue from a failed one programmatically, instead of inferring it from an empty string.\\n- Brings the GitHub/sqlite/memory backend path into conformance with `rules/silent-failure-prevention.md`, matching the correct behavior the beads backend already exhibits.\\n- Removes a specific, named instance of a write operation that doesn't report what changed \u2014 closing a documented gap rather than adding new speculative safeguards elsewhere.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T00:55:28.493550Z</sub>\\n\\n**Alignment assessment:** NOT_APPLICABLE\\n\\nThis is a pure defect fix to silent-failure behavior, not a feature proposal or architectural decision. The defect (backlog_add returning empty `item_ref` on GitHub issue creation failure with no error signal to the caller) directly violates the development-harness's standing `.claude/rules/silent-failure-prevention.md` convention\u2014specifically the rule that \\\"Every `if`/`elif` chain or match on an input value must have a final branch that either acts or errors\\\" (lines 40\u201367). \\n\\nFixing the violation aligns unambiguously with the product's mission: reliable, correct task management operations must report failures to their callers so that workflows (agents, CLI, MCP consumers) can respond appropriately. The fact-checked evidence shows:\\n- The beads backend already follows the correct pattern: it raises `ContentUnavailableError` on issue creation failure (test_backlog_core_operations.py, TestAddItemBeadsBackend)\\n- The GitHub/integer-ID backend violates the rule by returning empty string with no error signal\\n- The response model already has the `error` field designed for this signal (FallibleToolResponse inheritance)\\n\\nNo design tension exists between \\\"should a failed write operation report failure?\\\" and \\\"should it be silent?\\\" The answer for a production system is always the former. Grooming work is needed only on the *implementation detail*\u2014whether to raise, populate the `error` field, or use another mechanism\u2014not on whether to surface the failure.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T01:02:59.595359Z</sub>\\n\\n<details><summary>struck: 2026-09-04T01:32:16.754773Z \u2014 Architecture phase (plan/architect-backlog-add-silent-failure.md) found the originally groomed criteria contradict existing, currently-passing tests \u2014 correcting before task decomposition.</summary>\\n\\n- A `backlog_add` call (MCP tool) where GitHub issue creation fails or GitHub is unavailable surfaces a non-None, non-empty error/reason to the caller in the response \u2014 the caller can distinguish this outcome from a successful creation without inspecting `warnings` text.\\n- The CLI `backlog add` command exhibits the equivalent caller-visible signal for the same failure (no longer exits 0 with a bare `item_ref: \\\"\\\"` and no other indication of failure).\\n- The existing test `test_add_item_item_ref_empty_when_no_github_issue` (test_backlog_core_operations.py:419-431), which currently codifies `item_ref == \\\"\\\"` with no error as the entire signal, is updated to assert the corrected contract rather than continuing to assert today's silent-failure shape.\\n- Existing green-path tests for `backlog_add` / `add_item` (successful issue creation) still pass unchanged.\\n- `test_live_validation.py::test_l1_add_with_real_issue` and `test_l11_resolve_alternative_end` either pass, or \u2014 if issue creation genuinely fails in that environment \u2014 fail with a message that shows the real reason for the failure rather than an opaque empty-string/type-conversion error.\\n- The beads-backend behavior (`TestAddItemBeadsBackend`, already raising `ContentUnavailableError`) is unchanged.\\n</details>\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T01:32:16.754842Z</sub>\\n\\n- A `backlog_add` call (MCP tool) where a GitHub client was obtained but the issue-creation call itself raises (`GithubException`/`BacklogError`) surfaces a non-None, non-empty error/reason to the caller in the response \u2014 the caller can distinguish this outcome from a successful creation without inspecting `warnings` text.\\n- A `backlog_add` call where no GitHub client could be obtained at all (\\\"GitHub unavailable\\\") continues to succeed as a local-only item with `item_ref: \\\"\\\"` and no error \u2014 this is intentional, already-shipped degraded-mode behavior (#2999, `test_add_item_local_only_pending_state_visible_via_list_and_view`) and existing tests (`tests/test_frontend_parity_ops.py`'s `dh_env`-fixtured suite, which runs with `GITHUB_TOKEN=\\\"\\\"` against a SQLite backend and asserts CLI exit code 0) exercise exactly this path. Do not surface an error on this branch.\\n- The CLI `backlog add` command exhibits the equivalent caller-visible signal for the create-call-raised failure only (exit non-zero / stderr reason), not for the GitHub-unavailable branch.\\n- The existing test `test_add_item_item_ref_empty_when_no_github_issue` (test_backlog_core_operations.py:419-431) is reviewed against which branch it actually exercises and updated only if it covers the create-call-raised case; left unchanged if it exercises the GitHub-unavailable case.\\n- Existing green-path tests for `backlog_add`/`add_item` (successful issue creation) and the `dh_env`-fixtured parity suite (GitHub-unavailable, local-only creation) still pass unchanged.\\n- `test_live_validation.py::test_l1_add_with_real_issue` and `test_l11_resolve_alternative_end` either pass, or \u2014 if issue creation genuinely fails in that environment \u2014 fail with an assertion message that includes `result.get(\\\"error\\\")` so the real reason is visible.\\n- The beads-backend behavior (`TestAddItemBeadsBackend`, raising `ContentUnavailableError`) is unchanged by this item \u2014 a separate, pre-existing gap (neither `backlog_add` nor CLI `add` catches `ContentUnavailableError`, only `BacklogError`) is tracked as its own backlog item, not fixed here.\\n\\nCorrection (2026-09-04, post-architecture): the original criteria required surfacing an error on both \\\"creation fails\\\" and \\\"GitHub is unavailable.\\\" The unavailable branch is deliberate, already-shipped local-only-creation behavior \u2014 requiring an error there would break `tests/test_frontend_parity_ops.py`'s passing parity suite. See `plan/architect-backlog-add-silent-failure.md` concerns.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T01:02:59.595340Z</sub>\\n\\nWhen GitHub issue creation fails or GitHub is unavailable during `backlog_add` / `operations.add_item()` (integer-ID backend path: GitHub, sqlite, memory), the caller \u2014 whether the MCP tool or the CLI command \u2014 must be able to detect programmatically that creation did not succeed, and must be able to learn why (the reason text already captured today via `out.warn()`, but currently reaching no caller-visible failure signal). A response that looks identical to a successful creation (populated dict, empty `item_ref`, no error indicator) is not acceptable on this path. This describes the required outcome only; the specific contract shape (raising an exception, populating the existing `error` field, an explicit status field, or another mechanism) is explicitly deferred to planning, per the item's Description and the Design Intent Alignment section.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Effort\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T01:02:59.595433Z</sub>\\n\\nSmall. The defect is isolated to one function chain (`_try_create_github_issue` \u2192 `_try_create_backend_issue_ref` \u2192 `add_item`) shared by both production callers, so no per-caller duplication of work is expected. Test surface is bounded: one existing unit test needs updating to match the corrected contract, and two live E2E assertions should be re-verified. The one consumer doc only needs a change if the chosen contract shape requires callers to branch on a new signal.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Reproducibility\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T01:02:59.595239Z</sub>\\n\\nDeterministic given the triggering precondition (GitHub issue creation unavailable or failing) \u2014 not a flake. Evidence already established in Fact-Check/Description:\\n- 20+ consecutive identical CI failures on `main`; every E2E and Code Quality run has failed for at least four weeks (sampled 2026-07-28, 08-06, 08-10 through 08-23, all failures).\\n- Flake causes ruled out with evidence: fresh tmp dir + per-run UUID prefix + `force=True` per run; step completes in 12.4s with no 403/429 (not rate limiting or auth rejection); no leftover state or run contention.\\n- The defect predates PR #3160 (only the test's symptom text changed, not the underlying functions) and predates commit 765262e89 (2026-08-12), which introduced the `item_ref` field.\\n\\nSteps to reproduce: call `backlog_add` (MCP tool) or `backlog add` (CLI), on the GitHub/sqlite/memory backend path, under a condition where `_try_create_github_issue()` returns `None` (GitHub unavailable, or a `GithubException`/`BacklogError` during creation). Observed result: `item_ref` is `\\\"\\\"`, no error/exception is raised, and the response is otherwise shaped like a success \u2014 the only trace of the real reason is in `out.warn()` (surfaced as `warnings`, not `error`). The beads (string-ID) backend does not reproduce this \u2014 it already raises `ContentUnavailableError` on the equivalent failure.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Diagnosed from the E2E live tests failure on main, 2026-08-23\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Concerns\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T03:43:51.363173Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] `plugins/development-harness/skills/interop/SKILL.md` (lines 87-95) has a mermaid flow that calls `backlog_add` and branches `CheckError{Response has error key?}` \u2192 `Yes: ABORT`. Once this fix lands, `error` can be populated on a call where the item WAS still stored (creation-attempted-and-failed branch) \u2014 that ABORT would discard a successfully-stored item, the same contradiction T5 just fixed in `create/start.md`. Not in the original Impact Radius. (reported by dh:task-worker/dh:service-docs-maintainer on T5)\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T03:50:19.665433Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] CONTRACT VIOLATION at operations.py:1444 \u2014 expected `def _try_create_github_issue(...) -> tuple[int | None, str | None]`; actual `-> int | None`; function does not return error reason as second tuple element (reported by contract-verification on T1)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-09-04T00:56:25.635065Z</sub>\\n\\n**Root Cause:** `_try_create_backend_issue_ref()` (operations.py line 1499) silently converts `None` from `_try_create_github_issue()` into an empty string without surfacing the failure to the caller.\\n\\n**Failure Chain:**\\n1. **Source:** `_try_create_github_issue()` (operations.py:1444\u20131463) \u2014 called by `_try_create_backend_issue_ref()` on line 1498.\\n   - On `try_get_github(...) is None` (GitHub unavailable) \u2192 returns `None` at line 1458, records reason via `out.warn()` only (line 1457).\\n   - On caught `GithubException`/`BacklogError` \u2192 returns `None` at line 1463, records reason via `out.warn()` only (line 1462).\\n   - Result: The reason string is captured in `out` but not returned to the caller in any exception or error field.\\n\\n2. **Propagation:** `_try_create_backend_issue_ref()` (operations.py:1498\u20131499) converts `None` to empty string.\\n   - Line 1498: `issue_num = _try_create_github_issue(...)`\\n   - Line 1499: `return f\\\"#{issue_num}\\\" if issue_num else \\\"\\\"` \u2192 evaluates to `\\\"\\\"` when `issue_num` is `None`.\\n   - No error signal, no exception raised; the empty string is returned as a success-shaped result.\\n\\n3. **Lost Signal:** `add_item()` (operations.py:1528\u20131636) builds the response dict without populating `error`.\\n   - Lines 1626\u20131636 construct the response: `{\\\"title\\\": ..., \\\"priority\\\": ..., \\\"item_ref\\\": \\\"\\\", ...}`.\\n   - `BacklogAddResponse` inherits `error: str | None` from `FallibleToolResponse` (tool_responses.py:113\u2013117, 212), but it is left `None` because no exception was raised on the silent-failure path.\\n   - The `out.to_dict()` (which contains `warnings`/`errors` from `out.warn()` calls) is merged into the response, but the typed `error` field\u2014which callers expect for binary success/failure checks\u2014remains `None`.\\n\\n4. **Blind Spot:** MCP tool and CLI both inherit the blind spot.\\n   - MCP tool `backlog_add` (server.py:1377\u20131405) calls `operations.add_item`, then `_respond(BacklogAddResponse, {**result, **out.to_dict()})`; the typed `error` channel goes unused on this path.\\n   - CLI command `backlog add` (sam_schema/backlog.py:38\u201373) calls `operations.add_item` directly and exits 0 with `item_ref: \\\"\\\"` in the JSON payload, printing warnings to stderr but never raising or populating a failure indicator.\\n\\n**Evidence Chain (Fact-Check verified):**\\n- **Claim 1 (source verified):** operations.py lines 1444\u20131463 confirm `_try_create_github_issue` returns `None` on both failure modes (lines 1457, 1462 show `out.warn()` only).\\n- **Claim 2 (source verified):** operations.py line 1499 confirms empty-string conversion with no error signal.\\n- **Claim 3 (source verified):** tool_responses.py lines 113\u2013117 (FallibleToolResponse base class) and line 212 (BacklogAddResponse) show the unused `error` field.\\n- **Claim 4 (source verified):** PR #3160 changed test symptom text only; the functions at lines 1444\u20131499 are identical before and after; defect predates commit 765262e89 (Aug 12, 2026) when `item_ref` field was introduced.\\n- **Claim 5 (rule verified):** `rules/silent-failure-prevention.md:40\u201367` prohibits this pattern: \\\"Every branch must either act or error; falling through to return unchanged without logging is a silent data loss bug.\\\"\\n\\n**Precedent for Target Contract:** The beads (string-ID) backend path in `_try_create_backend_issue_ref()` (operations.py:1486\u20131497) already raises `ContentUnavailableError` when `create_beads_issue_for_item` fails (see test suite `TestAddItemBeadsBackend`); the integer-ID path should match this shape.\\n\\n**Test Surface:** `test_backlog_core_operations.py:419\u2013431` (`test_add_item_item_ref_empty_when_no_github_issue`) explicitly asserts today's contract (`result[\\\"item_ref\\\"] == \\\"\\\"`). This test **codifies the defect** and must be updated (not just supplemented) by any fix; it will start failing the moment the contract changes to raise or populate `error`.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"2d94c3920e25374e3045f43367fa94af09797470ebf907b91b4e52b2c5a1346e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABSe9fTw\"}"}